.TH FBMQ-MESSAGE 5 "February 2026" "fbmq 1.0.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
fbmq-message \- fbmq message file format
.SH DESCRIPTION
An
.B fbmq
message is a Markdown file (.md) with RFC 822 headers.
.SH FORMAT
.nf
Id: a3f2e1b4c5d6a7b8c9d0e1f2a3b4c5d6
Created-At: 2026-02-26T14:30:01.123456789Z
Created-By: 28431@worker-12
Priority: normal
Retry-Count: 0
TTL: 3600
Tags: orders, processing
Correlation-Id: req-abc-123
Custom:
  order_id: 12345

# Order Processing Request

Process order **12345**.
.fi
.SH FIELDS
.TP
.B id
(required) 128 bits of random entropy formatted as 32 hex characters.
.TP
.B created_at
(required) ISO 8601 with nanoseconds.
.TP
.B created_by
(required) Default: pid@hostname.
.TP
.B priority
critical | high | normal | low. Default: normal.
.TP
.B retry_count
Delivery attempts. Default: 0.
.TP
.B ttl
Seconds from created_at. 0 = no expiry.
.TP
.B tags
Comma-separated list of labels.
.TP
.B correlation_id
Workflow tracing ID.
.TP
.B custom
Arbitrary continuation lines. Passed through by the queue.
.SH FILENAME
.nf
a3f2e1b4c5d6a7b8c9d0e1f2a3b4c5d6.md

In processing/:
1740000001000000000.a3f2e1b4c5d6a7b8c9d0e1f2a3b4c5d6.md
^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
claim timestamp (seconds + 9-digit nanoseconds)
.fi
.SH HEADER FORMAT
fbmq uses RFC 822-style headers: field names are case-insensitive, separated
from values by a colon and space. Headers end at the first blank line.
Continuation lines (starting with whitespace) are supported under
.BR Custom: .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fbmq (1),
